summary: Provision a FreeIPA env and run its job recipe
description: |
    This test lives in the separate ci-freeipa repository; the plan in the
    FreeIPA repo under test discovers it from this repo at a pinned ref.
    Runs on a Testing Farm guest (or locally). The plan's prepare step
    installs the BuildRequires of freeipa.spec.in, so when no SRPM URL is
    supplied the test builds freeipa's SRPM directly on the guest: from a
    clone of FREEIPA_REPO_URL at FREEIPA_REPO_REF, or from the checkout
    given in FREEIPA_SRC (local runs). It bakes the batch's channel images
    from it ONCE, then runs every preset in the batch (FREEIPA_JOBS)
    through the same freeipa-env up/run/down flow a local or ssh queue job
    would, reusing the SRPM and channel images across presets. Exits with
    the worst per-job run status.
test: bash ./tf-runner.sh
duration: 12h
result: custom
